= a
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=a}

The <hidden subgroup problem> for a <group> $G$ is specified by an oracle $f:G\to S$ that hides an unknown <subgroup> $H\leq G$: it is constant on each left <coset> of $H$ and takes distinct values on distinct cosets. The task is to determine $H$, usually by finding a <generating set> for it.

= b
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

A shift-invariant basis is a common <eigenbasis> of all <cyclic shift operator>[cyclic shift operators] $U(\gamma)$. For the displayed Fourier states, <orthonormal set>[orthonormality] follows from the <root-of-unity filter>:
$$
\langle\xi_\alpha|\xi_{\alpha'}\rangle
=\frac1N\sum_{\beta\in\mathbb Z_N}
\omega^{(\alpha-\alpha')\beta}
=\delta_{\alpha,\alpha'}.
$$
There are $N$ vectors in this <orthonormal set> in the $N$-dimensional <Hilbert space>, so they form a <basis>. Reindexing the finite sum gives
$$
\begin{aligned}
U(\gamma)|\xi_\alpha\rangle
&=\frac1{\sqrt N}\sum_\beta
\omega^{-\alpha\beta}|\beta+\gamma\rangle\\
&=\omega^{\alpha\gamma}|\xi_\alpha\rangle.
\end{aligned}
$$
Thus every $|\xi_\alpha\rangle$ is simultaneously an <eigenvector> of every shift, with <eigenvalue> $\omega^{\alpha\gamma}$ for $U(\gamma)$.

= c
{parent=1}
